Title: "Hidden and Advanced Commands"
Id: "ccdec3fd-2e97-4ea0-b739-1f06956af40d"

Text: "The executable contains four commands that are intentionally omitted from
`mlg --help`. They support language development, issue reproduction, and one
easter egg; they are not part of the ordinary collection workflow.

```text
mlg debug
mlg extract ID
mlg report ID [ID...]
mlg whte_rbt.obj
```

`mlg debug` opens an interactive terminal UI for experimenting with formulation,
structural, and command-header parsers. It changes modes with the tab controls,
shows parser output or diagnostics for the entered text, and exits with its quit
key or an interrupt.

`mlg extract ID` loads and checks the current collection, locates the top-level
item with that exact `Id:`, and prints pasteable Mathlingua containing that item
and its transitive dependencies in dependency-first order. When the source
collection has check errors, those diagnostics follow the extracted source on
standard output so a single redirected result preserves the reproduction.

`mlg report ID [ID...]` builds the same self-contained extraction for one or
more items, places it in a Markdown issue template, and opens an editor. It
requires an interactive terminal. After previewing the edited issue, it asks
the user to report, edit again, or cancel; a blank response never submits. The
report action uses the `gh` CLI when available and otherwise opens a prefilled
GitHub issue form.

`mlg whte_rbt.obj` is a non-collection easter egg. It prints an animated terminal
sequence and then continues until interrupted; it performs no Mathlingua parsing
or checking."
Id: "f976d1ae-5a2c-471e-90cf-4be9d0940c0c"
